                                  EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT
    ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
    This employment contract (hereinafter the "Contract") is entered into by and between the NanoTrasen Corporation, represented by an authorized command representative (hereinafter the "Corporation"), and the undersigned employee (hereinafter the "Contractor"), as follows.

    ⠀[head=3]1. SUBJECT MATTER[/head]
    1.1. The Corporation hereby employs the Contractor aboard a NanoTrasen facility, and the Contractor undertakes to faithfully perform all service duties in accordance with this Contract, the NanoTrasen Corporate Law, Standard Work Procedures, and the Job Duty Form for the position held.
    1.2. Signing of this Contract is a mandatory condition of admission to duty in [color=#B22222]Security[/color]. The Contract takes effect upon signing by both parties and affixing of seals.

    ⠀[head=3]2. TERM[/head]
    2.1. This Contract covers the entire duration of the current work shift, regardless of its actual length.
    2.2. Shift start and end are determined solely by orders of Central Command or station command.
    2.3. This Contract automatically expires upon arrival of the evacuation shuttle at Central Command Station at shift end. Renewal for the next shift is effected by re-signing in the prescribed manner.

    ⠀[head=3]3. GENERAL INFORMATION[/head]
    3.1. Duty station of the Contractor: [color=#B22222]Security[/color].
    3.2. Main areas of activity: keeping order aboard the facility; protecting the lives and health of the crew as well as corporate property; enforcing Corporate Law; detaining and suppressing violators; guarding critical assets and restricted areas; investigating crimes and collecting evidence.

    ⠀[head=3]4. REMUNERATION[/head]
    4.1. For faithful performance of service duties, the Contractor is granted a salary per the current NanoTrasen rates for the position held.
    4.2. Wages are paid automatically by the NanoTrasen corporate payment system to the Contractor's personal identification card, in the manner and time established by internal corporate regulations.
    4.3. Bonuses are granted at station command's discretion for outstanding service to the Corporation.

    ⠀[head=3]5. SPECIAL TERMS[/head]
    5.1. The Contractor acknowledges that duty aboard NanoTrasen facilities involves increased risk to life and health, including but not limited to: depressurization, fires, radiation and anomalous exposure, unlawful acts of third parties. By signing this Contract, the Contractor confirms awareness of this fact and voluntary acceptance of all associated risks in full.
    5.2. Should the Contractor perish in the line of duty, the Corporation undertakes to provide cloning or other revival where technically possible and expedient.
    5.3. This Contract does not cover acts committed by the Contractor in violation of Corporate Law or Standard Work Procedures. The Contractor bears sole responsibility for such acts under the established procedure, up to and including unilateral termination of the Contract at the Corporation's initiative.
    5.4. All disputes arising from this Contract are resolved by station command with the involvement of the Legal Department, or, failing that, by Central Command. Decisions of Central Command are final and not subject to appeal.

    ⠀[head=3]6. SIGNATURES[/head]
    This Contract is drawn up in two counterparts of equal legal force, one for each party.
    By signing this Contract, the Contractor confirms familiarity with its contents, the NanoTrasen Corporate Law, and the Job Duty Form for the position held, and accepts all terms of this Contract in full, without any reservations or exceptions.

    Employee signature: [sign=1] [sign_limit=1]

